<title>USA: Nalco Chemical completes IWC acquisition.</title>
<headline>Nalco Chemical completes IWC acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>NAPERVILLE, Ill. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nalco Chemical Co said Wednesday it completed its acquisition of International Water Consultants Beheer B.V. (IWC), based in Maarssen, Netherlands.</p>
<p>Terms of the transaction were not disclosed.</p>
<p>IWC was a wholly owned subsidiary of Servo Delden B.V., a company of Greman-based  Huls AG.</p>
<p>IWC provides water treatment services in various European countries. It had 1996 sales of about $20 million.</p>
<p>Nalco provides water treatment and process chemicals and services.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
